[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've put three filter placements in a browser tab:
  [94m]8;id=bgc1nx;http://localhost:65374/?key=492b1bd9ef84f40a349cf09e9bb6e7be68c6ee59fc86113350568d514a8429d9\http://localhost:65374/?key=492b1bd9ef84f40a349cf09e9bb6e7be68c6ee59fc86113350568d514a8429d9[39m]8;;\

  - [1mA. Filter bar above the table.[0m An event type select, a date range select and a "Failed sign-ins only" checkbox, all
    visible all the time, with a line like "Showing 4 of 52 events" below them.
  - [1mB. Quick views plus event type.[0m A radio group with four views (All, Failed sign-ins, Sign-ins and sign-outs, Account
    changes) and an event type select next to it.
  - [1mC. Filters button.[0m A button opens a panel with the filter controls, and active filters show as tags you can remove.

  I recommend A. Failed sign-ins are one click away, and security says that's what people come to this page for. It also
  uses only plain labelled form fields and keeps the diff small.

  Take a look and tell me what you think here. You can also click an option in the browser to select it.

  I haven't changed any code yet. I'll bring these to you before the design is final:
  - [1mPage is empty without JavaScript.[0m Today [38;5;153mactivity.js[39m builds every table row, which breaks the standing rule that
    pages stay readable with JavaScript off.
  - [1mNo shared token sheet found.[0m I haven't found the file the guidelines' tokens come from.
  - [1mExisting CSS uses raw values.[0m [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m already has raw hex and px values; I need to know how much of it to
    convert to tokens.
  - [1mTime zone not shown.[0m Event times don't say what zone they're in.

  Separately, [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, so the sketch files would show up in [38;5;153mgit status[39m. I'd suggest adding it.

